# Board rotation controls and compact bottom labels

Add left/right quarter-turn controls to the Board and keep every bottom-bar label on one line.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] The Board screen shows a circular-arrow-left action and a circular-arrow-right action.
- [x] In view mode, the burger menu, rotate-left, and rotate-right controls sit side by side at the upper-left, in that order.
- [x] In edit mode, both rotation controls remain available together beneath the Terrain/Numbers selector.
- [x] Tapping left rotates the board view 90 degrees counter-clockwise.
- [x] Tapping right rotates the board view 90 degrees clockwise.
- [x] Four repeated rotations in either direction return to the original orientation without cumulative geometry drift.
- [x] Rotation applies consistently in view and edit modes, including terrain, numbers, roads, buildings, ghosts, and interaction targets.
- [x] Rotation does not mutate the underlying logical board coordinates or saved board state.
- [x] The selected orientation persists across Board navigation and application termination as part of the active game.
- [x] A fresh game resets orientation to its default.
- [x] Existing pan, zoom, tap-to-focus, and hold/radial editing remain correct in every orientation.
- [x] Edit, Hand, and Analysis bottom-bar labels use smaller fonts and fit comfortably on one line.
- [x] Controls have distinct accessible labels and identifiers.
- [x] Geometry/unit and UI regression coverage compile.
- [ ] Focused rotation and compact-layout checks pass on a functioning simulator or device.

## Evidence

- Added a four-state, Codable quarter-turn orientation to the active-game snapshot with legacy `.north` fallback and fresh-game default.
- Added left/right model transitions and applied the orientation to the complete interactive Board layer without changing logical coordinates.
- Positioned accessible menu/left/right controls in view mode and retained the rotation pair below the edit-mode picker.
- Added four-turn/no-drift and serialization unit coverage plus UI control-order coverage.
- Reduced bottom action labels to single-line caption text with compact scaling.
- Arm64 simulator-target `xcodebuild build-for-testing` succeeded.
